{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0038e0d1f4aca2898132cc91cacf76cd27e62c1f7fdc5edcbf87b2b7754d2f54","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f40f621fa58f753ffd58aa666dd6caf253ad7b4712620247572b2eee1e24d4e6"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"R2E-Gym is presented as a procedurally curated gym environment for training real-world SWE agents, with over 8.1K problems across 13 repos including executable environments, unit tests, and natural-language task descriptions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_22c6037214ff8457abe117e18e2f6c1e400b0746b230638c66fe6b6006e38d5a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_046da95987dae646a13ff74dbff1f3a1a95c8e69ecbd585450839b54c572e6ea","slc_0c8f5900583f16bbdc7dc4160bae5c7978a99d0cd53c9ea016404d93dbb84098","slc_114431affd6eecb7676888a4668594f54ef99a703d30a87e1bff1f054532777e","slc_303322c5bbcc1e9a92bddc66aba4252aac50ad19b352c6abc8a238c6511c8be1","slc_344a62ffa64b52731edcf30422e91450f3f8260f82c2483222bdd747f34bca9c","slc_5030764fdb2e36238e99fb3c2bd0f038662cc94ff9974e71a9edf94948222201","slc_b1ea41ef3c0803bfa7e10d16cce80bfe37ebedbe32986f9e509df58d6b8a74d1","slc_cd27e045faa0515ff9325b35d4584ff046acd46e4a1721afbf7c9a2584097bf3"],"source_ids":["src_95d7344beaf754a299b7206f98d4892b"],"text":"Environment generation follows a documented pipeline: register the repo in constants and a RepoName enum with a test command, add it as a git submodule, collect and filter commits (bug-fix, test-matching, test-entity edits), then validate with Docker-based installation and test execution.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_27965e66a0f070d8bacf7a2014c3a18f4fe657305378424f1f5211f39ef7041c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_06a0a9923a9009e9ae82ac09be6339843102b5181a11acaef91e457894a89eca","slc_4aaf1f98830dc83afd7cfee4a53da2729203c58c7e90221afbbc0e8ceddafddd","slc_70a14bb8a61d9516a84e2be1e77410f9ad0c00e4a9531d4f4bd09a051379d23a","slc_f8ad4fb7c004f52dd8bb8a43b2665db857c295a42919fd9afeeeef8c422e64a5"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"Agent training is done with LLaMA-Factory using provided config files (e.g., llamafactory-cli train train/train_r2egym_32B_agent.yaml), with optional faster-training dependencies like flashattention2, deepspeed, liger-kernel, and unsloth.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2a78f6b2e2fa5cb4ae62e73bb23d1a27088055b133737c559a680e54e8eff004","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b1b3700088998de1eb07e84a66455e643ff37b172d3bc3d3d02c746f85265045"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"The SWE-GEN recipe curates executable training environments from commits rather than human-written pull requests or unit tests, which the authors say enables more scalable data curation and agent training.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_320a8ee4b12b7adff5a77e9936d6d8d08aeca0c003309ed56bf699883cc534a7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a209de11d6d2e8d5616f8edfaa9808d7c62f950f7e36f158bbd18b2d4dc9ac30","slc_b1b3700088998de1eb07e84a66455e643ff37b172d3bc3d3d02c746f85265045","slc_dd1c0a4ccf92c692a29578b730e416f5045c5a605664f173fcaa80aea26ef346"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"The README reports benchmark results: 51% pass@1 on SWE-Bench Verified with hybrid test-time scaling and 34.4% pass@1 for the commit-based curation approach, both claimed as state-of-the-art for open-weight SWE agents.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6492ad663eb6d55b551f021a0cef2fdba426c9eaf4fb8b5fc967e8bcbc57da54","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_30ee963b0b6e6d42022815324abdb885afc5687d16bef81a20d890c5dd33cffb"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"The repo's own evaluation command only produces output trajectories and patches; final SWE-Bench scores are obtained with the official SWE-Bench evaluation harness.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_691ef8969fad957caf6b3d9c62b23d5e4b0f3351d3ab55df03035f9ddd372ea6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1a9699ed3eee89ab91ceaefb9175598a8eb768769e80fd1551af6a0e33dbd3a9","slc_1d1227a7182ddb848ab353c7dcc6137734f9975c615ce91711e3ca6b29a13c10","slc_5afa7ab0395a758e69d3e945e033a786a6957337b6d567602d068dd16fd3261c","slc_8efdf303cac97f085023ee0380e0924d1b41378311a6388fca049cab1b9db3e4","slc_fdb9c61c3a4dcdd02b57a3a05ef637ce57a4d5e54a10171225291a7962503e55"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"Environments support automated reward calculation via env.runtime._calculate_reward() using unit tests, plus helpers such as apply_patch, get_gt_commit, and reverse_patch, and env.get_stats() for per-environment metadata.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7109bf6fe3a687b1da02d2a3436cd0d52ea85ffc014e625c6ba30c60f79054e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d68ba381c8653243eb58a2fc9bc655335794b553da467eb9b09a8715a2f1193d"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"Trajectory collection and evaluation support parallelized inference via runagent_multiple with --max_workers (e.g., 54 workers), and each gym instance uses a Docker image of roughly 300-500MB.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b04ee9d2bc1f1174733a7f39f90ff344b5c0dadbacd4ed583aab58f8269effe2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e1d76e44698d823e74a11746047708d82a1ed2f461284a2313e2d5d7aca1f39a"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"Agent runs return a Trajectory object containing the full agent trajectory, problem statement, max execution time, exit reason, and output patch.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b3079e72100b30c8ceb09f7c23b92046eaea0c0a4963d7065a915b2a2e2524e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a209de11d6d2e8d5616f8edfaa9808d7c62f950f7e36f158bbd18b2d4dc9ac30","slc_b2ae28150949e93079247c9139c56b2cac95d3d1203a7c7c076bf9d0c0394cd4"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"Hybrid Test-time Scaling combines execution-based and execution-free verifiers, described as having complementary strengths and weaknesses, to achieve better performance when scaling test-time compute.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b92fc9d3d0712fa090da61ecf9b50f9119ac19d177b37020dc00cac42e888b02","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fb19c24a529ef03e4da0b0bd3fec8b07a09a5566c00309f6cb7f519389fd3293"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"Precollected SFT trajectories are provided for three agent types: a general-purpose code editing agent, an execution-based testing agent generating targeted unit tests, and an execution-free verifier agent for training-free patch reranking.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d71cf33803093d7e55fe61adfd646e9b3e60ff7e0abf26ecadb1c01991200f52","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4f8d63db738d42db7151ac8e8960286073fcacbfe29df0847c24c16e854e679c","slc_cf55a6491807f4c44fce2c63fa48244d8c717c77b7a7de8e6dfd5d856b83dab6","slc_d68ba381c8653243eb58a2fc9bc655335794b553da467eb9b09a8715a2f1193d","slc_f45d9dc3f92dac8dd5fdf71d3c1f30e69093b93f43f458049b55b36a4c24d118"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"The project uses uv for environment management (venv creation and sync), and agent runs can target LLMs including claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022, gpt-4o, or a vLLM-served R2EGym-32B-Agent model.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","created_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fd9de2c267f06d54ee8715e61b9df43b676325b52834ba688c121d3acb4b5ffd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"r2e-gym/r2e-gym@0d94c4eb9431 snapshot ea915f385f175d1e","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_05e5a31c851e29bc91cd4be489de3cc514caa84cc3611d371803b0387ccae13e","slc_2b5bcbdfaba510d6148d6d439eaf8fa594547024b4de0b717c361d8c58962d27","slc_7bf905d076148f5c86d85009762aacbc49cd3bf191e652dbe6ba1690ff8f5c9b","slc_cf55a6491807f4c44fce2c63fa48244d8c717c77b7a7de8e6dfd5d856b83dab6"],"source_ids":["src_d8e2c60d433f54849c3561da377b87f5"],"text":"The Python API exposes EnvArgs and RepoEnv from r2egym.agenthub.environment.env and AgentArgs/Agent from r2egym.agenthub.agent.agent; an agent is run via agent.run(env, max_steps=40, use_fn_calling=True).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:17:34Z","updated_by_operation":"op_cce33fe711e94e509fbe06d4a2c67152"}
